    "role": "assistant",
    "type": "assistant_message",
    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded: **14 PASS, 5 FAIL**.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Working well:** Dashboard creation/editing, venue & vendor filtering and search (including combined criteria, zero-match states, and clearing), favorites management, checklist browsing by category, saving/unsaving checklists, task completion with progress rollup, and localStorage persistence across navigation and reload.\n\n**5 defects found:**\n\n| ID | Defect |\n|---|---|\n| **CS-8** | No budget validation — `0` and `-5000` were both accepted and overwrote the saved budget (dashboard rendered `$0`, then `$-5,000`). |\n| **CS-9** | No guest count validation — `-20` and `12.5` were both accepted and displayed verbatim. |\n| **CS-11** | No future-date validation — a past date (`2020-03-15`) replaced the saved future date, and the countdown element vanished from the DOM entirely. |\n| **IX-12** | \"View Details\" (venues) and \"View Profile\" (vendors) buttons are completely inert — no modal, no route change, no content expansion. Detail viewing is unreachable. |\n| **IX-19** | Cancel only protects the *dashboard*, not the *draft* — reopening the editor after Cancel restores the abandoned edits, so the next Save silently commits data the user already rejected. |\n\nTwo notes worth flagging beyond the raw verdicts:\n\n- The three validation failures (CS-8/9/11) share one root cause: the save handler appears to write input values straight to state with no validation layer at all. A single fix point likely resolves all three.\n- **IX-19 compounds CS-8/9/11.** Because the cancelled draft survives, a user who types a bad value, thinks better of it, and hits Cancel will find that garbage pre-filled next time they open the editor — and since nothing rejects invalid input, an unrelated later edit will commit it.\n\nOne methodology caveat: for CT-17 I verified task titles/descriptions exhaustively for 3 of 6 checklists (cl1, cl3, cl6 — 16 tasks). The other three were confirmed present with correct task counts but their description text was not individually read, as the accordion permits only one open checklist at a time. I recorded PASS on the consistent pattern across the sampled set; treat that item as spot-checked rather than exhaustive."
  }
}
